From f637c41894c38fbc6e74268dccf4ca0c63283f07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Oct 2023 15:27:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0179/1695] clk: stm32mp: add support of pinctrl and clock for
 RCC node

Add a generic stm32mp clock driver to support the OP-TEE initialization of
pinctrl and clock defined in the RCC sub-node with compatible "st,rcc".

This driver is used to configure in the board device tree the required
RCC resources as:
- pincontrol to manage Micro-controller clock output (MCO) pins,
  for example to provide this MCO clock on external device
- critical clocks, not managed by other drivers in OP-TEE

This sub-node is optional and avoids to manage the OP-TEE specific
compatibles "st,stm32mp13-rcc-mco" and "st,stm32mp15-rcc-mco",
with a more acceptable binding.

The configuration for this sub node is only done when the early DT drivers
are available, the clock provider (SoC RCC driver) and the pin-controller.

I also align the binding file with kernel one.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 055729e3b01b6e5b6629d442c45ff9d9802a58bc clk: stm32mp: add support of pinctrl and clock for RCC node]
